  "title": "Sappho",
  "summary": "Sappho of Lesbos was an Archaic Greek lyric poet whose verses gave voice to intense personal emotions, romantic love, and female desire. Celebrated throughout antiquity as the Tenth Muse and inventor of the Sapphic stanza, she composed nine volumes of monody that circulated across the Greek Mediterranean, establishing enduring literary standards despite surviving mostly in papyrus fragments.",
